# Level 17 with two players, and the ice weapon in the *second* player's hands.
#
# `movies/level17-weapon.zmv` is this route walked by player one; this is the
# same four moves walked by player two, who starts 46 px to the right at
# (330,420) and so needs a longer first leg. Player one does nothing at all.
#
# **What it is for is bit 15 of Y.** `$81:849B  TYA : ASL A : AND #$0000 :
# ROL A : ROL A` turns the sign of the raw collision id into the doubled side,
# and $80:9D6A turns that into the score slot whose MONSTER FROZEN tally gets
# the credit. With one player every id is positive, so reading the side off A --
# or off anything else that happens to be positive -- passes every call. Here
# every shot is $805D, and the same perturbation fails at $7E:1FE0.
#
# It is `movies/level25-2p.zmv`'s finding one routine over: a coverage table
# counts branches, and which *value* went down a branch is not a branch. The
# pair of sites freeze_slot_0 and freeze_slot_1 is what names the gap, and it
# takes both movies to fill it -- one player each.
#
# Retune by watching where it actually gets to:
#   zamn_headless <rom> shot.png 3200 -m movies\level17-2p-freeze.zmv --records 2900,3100,200
